journal" publication-format="online"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>14. Romei</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Elisei</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinchera</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ceccherini</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Molinaro</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mancusi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Martino</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Romeo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Pacini</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Somatic mutations of the ret protooncogene in sporadic medullary thyroid carcinoma are not restricted to exon 16 and are associated with tumor recurrence</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>1996</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>1619</fpage><lpage>1622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8636377</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" publication-format="online"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>15. Pelizzo</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Boschin</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernante</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Toniato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Piotto</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pagetta</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Nibale</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Rampin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Muzzio</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubello</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Natural history, diagnosis, treatment and outcome of medullary thyroid cancer: 37 ye